    "title": "Meridian Arrows",
    "summary": "Two arrows closing on each other, drawn in theme tokens over whatever surface it is dropped onto.",
    "description": "Two arrows closing on each other, drawn in theme tokens over whatever surface it is dropped onto. Each covers half the gap along the axis their facing edges already share, and the pair is one vector: a data attribute flips its sign rather than declaring a second one, so the two can never be edited out of agreement. The spring is damped on purpose. Wound tighter the shapes carry into a near collision and read as a miss being corrected, landing flat loses the weight, so they settle a little way past the mark. The drawing is held at its resting angle as a static attribute rather than a transform, which keeps the travel in the drawing's own coordinates whatever angle the pair is turned to. One svg and one stylesheet, no dependencies and no client hooks, and the closing drops out under prefers-reduced-motion.",
